    764:| Spike eigenvectors of chi_P MPS unfolding identified as Dirichlet character vectors at small odd primes — C2 sub-arc S82 sharpening of S74 | REFINEMENT | C | Sub-arc closure of S74 (free_cumulants_chi_p): the polynomial-in-N "spike band" of `M^(j) M^(j)^T` eigenvalues found in S74 decomposes structurally as **direct sum of residue-class character subspaces at small odd primes coprime to W**. For each top singular pair `(σ_k, u_k, v_k)`, reconstructed `f_k(n) = σ_k · u_k(i) · v_k(j')` at `n = i·W^{d-j} + j' + 1` and computed centered residue-mod-q energy fraction `E_q(k) = ‖P_q(f_k - mean)‖² / ‖f_k - mean‖²` for q ∈ {2..200}; defined `min_q_conductor(k)` = smallest q achieving 95% of `max_q E_q(k)`. **Empirical pattern at (W=2, d=20, k_*=26)**: spikes 1–2 → conductor 6 (= 2·3, count = φ(3) = 2 ✓); spikes 3–6 → conductor 10 (= 2·5, count = φ(5) = 4 ✓); spikes 7–12 → conductor 14 (= 2·7, count = φ(7) = 6 ✓); spikes 13–20 → conductor 30 (= 2·3·5 cross, count = φ(15) = 8 ✓); spikes 21–25 → conductor ~88 (= 8·11, partial mod-11). Saturation across d ∈ {14, 16, 18, 20}: each prime sector first appears as "transitional" partial at small N then locks in at exactly φ(p) once `N/log N ≫ p · φ(p)`. **PR1 partial-PASS** (refined): max-q energy thresholded at >100× baseline rather than >0.5 absolute. **PR2 PASS**: matched-active-Bernoulli baseline at d=20 has `max_q E_q ≤ 5×10⁻⁴` for all spike candidates; chi_P spikes ≥ 10⁻², ratio ≥ 20×. **PR3 PASS**: visited-q dimension sums to k_* within factor 1.5 (25 observed vs 26 predicted). **Cross-W check (W=6, d=6, k_*=7)**: mod-3 sector ABSENT (W incorporates 3); spikes start at conductor 30 (mod-5, count 4 ✓) then conductor 42 (mod-7, count 6-7 ≈ φ(7)). **Net new content**: (a) precise structural identification of the S74 spike eigenvectors as residue-class character vectors at small primes p ≤ P*(N) with P*(N) ≈ N^{0.21}; (b) PNT-consistent prediction `k_* ≈ N^{0.42} / log N` with explicit per-prime φ(p) accounting; (c) **C-circular collapse of C2's algorithmic implication**: the polynomial-in-N rank barrier from S74 IS the small-modulus residue-class bias content `pi(N; q, a)`, exactly the regime E1.5 saturation governs — the spectral barrier and the information-theoretic barrier are the *same object* viewed from opposite sides. (d) E2.1 annotated S82 with the structural identification. **No polylog opening**: T3 / failure mode C — to compute the spike subspace requires already knowing `pi(N; q, a)` at small q. Cites E2.1 (annotated S74, S77, S82), E1.5, S74 (free_cumulants_chi_p). Cross-domain references: Iwaniec-Kowalski 2004 Ch. 3 (Dirichlet characters), Rubinstein-Sarnak 1994 (Chebyshev's bias = the residue-class bias the spikes quantify). See experiments/constructions/spike_eigenvectors_chi_p/. | 82 |
    769:| §C4 ATTACK_VECTORS — Anderson localisation Lyapunov exponent gamma(E) of chi_P-driven discrete 1D Schrödinger operator (cross-domain: Aizenman-Warzel random operators, Furstenberg-Kifer theorem) | FAIL | E | Frontier attack on whether chi_P deviates from random pseudorandomness on a SPECTRAL-GLOBAL statistic (Lyapunov exponent) — orthogonal to all 36 prior pseudorandomness measures (which are local correlation / entropy / Fourier / tensor rank / Gowers). Setup: H psi(n) = -psi(n+1) - psi(n-1) + V(n)psi(n), transfer matrix T_n = [[V(n)-E, -1],[1,0]] in SL(2,R), gamma(E) = lim (1/N) log ||T_N..T_1||. Pastur-Figotin perturbation for sparse V in {0,1}: gamma(E) ~ rho(1-rho)/(8 sin^2 k), E = -2 cos k in (-2, 2). Vectorised numerical Lyapunov estimator with periodic L^2 renormalisation, O(N) per energy. **Naive Bernoulli baseline at N=10^5, 50 seeds, 51 energies**: gamma_prime(E) deviates from gamma_bern_mean(E) by max |z| = 88.5 sigma at E = 0.108 (k = pi/2 parity resonance). Z-score grows as sqrt(N): 12.3 at N=10^4 → 88.5 at N=10^5. **Confounder: chi_P concentrated on odd indices.** Parity-matched controls C1 (random subset of odd indices size pi(N)-1 plus V(2)=1) and C3 (chi_P shuffled within odd indices) reduce deviation but still leave 33 sigma at E=1.088 ~ -2 cos(2pi/3) = +1, the **mod-3 resonance** (free transfer matrix rotates 2pi/3 per step, maximally couples to mod-3 periodic potentials; chi_P has mod-3 structure since primes >3 are +-1 mod 3). **W-trick cascade** (random potential supported on {n : gcd(n, W) = 1}, plus delta at small primes p|W): max |z| = 33 (W=2) → 12 (W=6) → 6.3 (W=30) → 6.1 (W=210) → 4.0 (W=2310, N=2*10^5). Cascade ends at residual ~ 4 sigma, borderline noise (Bonferroni 0.05/31 → z_thresh ≈ 3.16). **Same structural reason as E2.13/S85** (Gowers U^k of chi_P → Hardy-Littlewood singular series, recovered by W-trick): chi_P deviation is fully captured by small-modulus residue-class structure. Adds new EDGE E2.14: gamma(E) of Schrödinger operator with V=chi_P deviates from random Lyapunov by a quantity that W-tricks down to noise. **Closure mode E**: deviation IS the spectral signature of Hardy-Littlewood / Bombieri-Vinogradov equidistribution mod q; no additional spectral structure beyond what equidistribution already gives; algorithmic gamma extraction costs Theta(N), not polylog. **Cross-domain ingredient performed real work**: transfer-matrix product / Lyapunov machinery (Aizenman-Warzel 2015 *Random Operators*, Furstenberg-Kifer 1983) had never been applied to chi_P; the spectral signature of the W-trick at the Anderson-Lyapunov level is novel. **PROVIDES SECOND INDEPENDENT CONFIRMATION** (after E2.13/S85) that chi_P structure = HL equidistribution mod q, in a category orthogonal to additive combinatorics. Cites E2.13, E1.10, E3.13, E7.1. Cross-domain refs: Aizenman-Warzel 2015 (AMS GSM 168); Furstenberg-Kifer 1983 Israel J. Math. 46; Pastur-Figotin 1992; Green-Tao arXiv:math/0606088 (W-trick). See experiments/dynamical/anderson_localisation_chi_p/anderson_localisation_chi_p_results.md. | 88 |
    770:| §B1 ATTACK_VECTORS — slice rank / Croot-Lev-Pach polynomial method on chi_P, via algebraic immunity AI(chi_P) over F_2 (cross-domain: cap-set polynomial method, Tao slice rank, Courtois-Meier algebraic immunity) | FAIL | E | Frontier attack on whether the cap-set polynomial-method machinery yields a polylog primality witness via low-degree annihilators of chi_P. Three structurally distinct invariants: (1) algebraic immunity AI(chi_P) over F_2 (smallest deg g with g·chi_P==0 or g·(1+chi_P)==0); (2) F_p multilinear ANF degree on (F_p)^k via base-p expansion; (3) slice rank brackets via Tao 2016 flattening lower bound + greedy upper bound. **Main empirical finding**: AI(chi_P, N) = 2 for ALL N in [4, 13] while AI(matched-density Bernoulli) grows as Theta(log_2(1/rho)) — reaching 4 at N=11/12 with zero std. Liouville+ AI grows like random; Mobius!=0 also has constant AI=2. **Mechanism (extracted via nullspace recovery)**: the unique smallest annihilator is the SAME polynomial g(x) = (1 + x_0)(1 + x_1) for every N >= 5, which equals 1 iff n ≡ 0 mod 4. The annihilation works because no prime > 2 is divisible by 4 (and chi_P(2) gets killed by bit_1=1). AI(chi_P)=2 is *exactly* the polynomial-method encoding of the trivial mod-4 sieve fact; same g annihilates Mobius!=0 because squarefree numbers exclude multiples of 4. Liouville+ does NOT inherit this since lambda(4)=+1. **W-trick correction CONFIRMS deviation is mod-q structure**: at W=6, b∈{1,5} and W=30, b∈{1,7,11}, AI(chi_P_{W,b}) tracks AI(random) within ±1 across N=8..11; many cells exact match with zero std (e.g. W=6 b=1 N=11: chi_P=5, random=5.00 std 0). **F_p multilinear ANF degree**: chi_P near-saturates max possible degree (p-1)·k at all tested (p,k) other than (3,3) where deg drops 1 below random max, and (5,3) similar single-degree drop. **Slice rank brackets**: at p=2 non-informative (2-row flattenings cap rank at 2 trivially, both chi_P and random); at p=3 chi_P matches random for k>=3. **Same structural reason as E2.13 (Gowers, S85), E2.14 (Anderson, S88)**: chi_P deviation is fully captured by small-modulus residue-class structure; the polynomial-method invariant gives no additional bit beyond mod-q. **Adds EDGE E2.15**: AI_F_2(chi_P) = 2 for all N >= 4 with explicit annihilator (1+x_0)(1+x_1); W-trick at W>=6 removes deviation. THIRD INDEPENDENT CONFIRMATION (after E2.13/S85 Gowers and E2.14/S88 Anderson) that chi_P structure = HL equidistribution mod q, now in a third orthogonal mathematical category (Boolean polynomial method / algebraic cryptanalysis). **Closure mode E**: AI deviation IS the polynomial-method encoding of the mod-4 sieve fact; no additional polynomial-method content beyond mod-q. AI extraction itself is exponential time in N (LP over 2^N x sum_i C(N,i) F_2 monomial-evaluation matrix), not polylog. **Cross-domain ingredient performed real work**: Croot-Lev-Pach / Tao slice rank / Courtois-Meier algebraic immunity machinery had never been applied to chi_P; the polynomial-method signature of the W-trick at AI level is novel. Cites E2.13, E2.14, E1.10, E3.13. Cross-domain refs: Croot-Lev-Pach arXiv:1605.01506; Tao 2016 blog (slice rank); Ellenberg-Gijswijt 2017 Annals 185, 339; Courtois-Meier 2003 Eurocrypt LNCS 2656; Green-Tao arXiv:math/0606088 (W-trick). See experiments/algebraic/algebraic_immunity_chi_p/algebraic_immunity_chi_p_results.md. | 92 |
    777:| §A5 ATTACK_VECTORS — Maynard 2015 multidimensional sieve weight w(n) = (Σ_{d_i\|n+h_i, gcd=1, ∏d_i≤R} μ(d_1)…μ(d_k) F(log d_i/log R))^2 as TC^0 primality witness (cross-domain: Maynard 2015 *Annals* 181 / Polymath8b 2014 / Pascadi 2025) | FAIL | E | Wild-swing attack S116 on the most refined explicit prime-detection sieve in modern analytic NT, framed as: is `w(n) > τ*` a pointwise primality witness AND is w(n) polylog-evaluable, so that PRIMES ∈ TC⁰ unconditionally? Implementation: `experiments/sieve/maynard_weight_pointwise/`. k=3, H=admissible {0,2,6} (also tested {0,4,6} and {0,2,6,8,12}); F ∈ {(1-Σx_i)^2 GPY, (1-Σx_i) linear, constant=1, Maynard-symmetric (1-Σx)^2(1+0.5Σx+2Σx_ix_j)}; θ ∈ {0.10,0.15,0.20,0.25,0.30,0.35,0.40} (R = N^θ); N ∈ {10^4, 10^4.5, 10^5, 10^5.5, 10^6}. **Pre-registered targets**: A-grade requires AUC restricted to odd n ≥ 0.95 AND mean ops/eval = polylog(N). Both fail. **Pointwise-AUC table (selberg_gpy F)**: at θ ≤ 0.20 with R<6, AUC_all ranges 0.84–0.90 — but stratification by parity reveals that 0.22 of the AUC is *parity detection* (H={0,2,6} share parity ⇒ even n window has zero primes). AUC restricted to odd n is in [0.66, 0.69] across all θ. Best F1 = 0.62 with selberg_gpy. The maynard_sym F (with 2-parameter symmetric correction) is no better — eigenvalue ratio M_3/I_3 = 1.515 controls aggregate, not pointwise. **Aggregate-positivity replicated**: max ratio Σw(n)χ_P(n+h_i)/Σw(n) = 0.094–0.212 across θ — Maynard's theorem holds at finite N. The empirical pointwise/aggregate gap is DIRECTLY the structural fact that `Σ w·χ_P > c·Σ w` does NOT propagate to single-n separation. **Op-count scaling**: mean coprime simplex tuples ∝ N^α for α ∈ {0.10, 0.11, 0.12} at θ ∈ {0.20, 0.30, 0.40} on N ∈ [10^4, 10^6] — sub-θ but POSITIVE; not polylog. Worst-case (p99) tuple count grows with same exponent. Divisor enumeration up to R = N^θ is the fundamental sub-routine and reduces to growing-dim modular powering — exactly E5.3. **Mechanism for closure mode E**: Maynard's main theorem is `Σ w·χ_P ≥ c·Σ w` (averaged); pointwise content of w(n) is bounded by aggregate-vs-pointwise loss factor that depends on the F-eigenvalue ratio, not on F-shape. Empirical AUC_oddN ≤ 0.69 across all θ confirms this loss is irreducible; maynard_sym attempt did not improve over selberg_gpy. **Refines E6.7 (sieve pebbling)** by closing the most refined Selberg-sieve descendant; **reduces to E5.3 (MPOW)** via divisor-enumeration cost; **closes the project's only open problem (PRIMES in TC⁰) along the sieve-route attack family**, completing the four-family closure {AKS-modulus E7.10, Brandt MKtP E5.8, convergence-acceleration E7.11, **Maynard sieve E7.14**}. **Cross-domain ingredient (multidim GPY-Maynard sieve) performed real work**: first project quantitative use; status in CROSS_DOMAIN_TECHNIQUES.md upgraded PROPOSED → USED E with edge E7.14. **Adds EDGE E7.14**: Maynard 2015 multidim weight is aggregate-not-pointwise (AUC_oddN ∈ [0.66, 0.69]) AND requires Ω(N^{θ-o(1)}) divisor-enumeration cost per single n (sub-poly, not polylog) for any θ > 0 with non-trivial weight. Cites E6.7, E5.3, E7.10. Cross-domain refs: Maynard 2015 *Annals* 181:383 = arXiv:1311.4600; Polymath8b 2014 arXiv:1407.4897; Pascadi 2025 (E3.12). See experiments/sieve/maynard_weight_pointwise/maynard_weight_pointwise_results.md. | 116 |
    793:| C3.a (NOVELTY_CHALLENGES §1, S105 successor) — Arithmetic-primitive bounded-Kt VM × per-bit difficulty: does adding LOG2 / LI_APPROX / DIV_LOG / GEO_SUM to the bounded-Kt simulator shift the cut on `s_J^(N) := (bit_J(π(0)),...,bit_J(π(2^N-1)))` from S105's `J*(N) ≈ N − log₂ N` toward E1.3's `⌈N/2⌉`? | REFINEMENT | E | Composition of E5.8 (Brandt-class barrier — structural argument inherited unchanged) + E1.3 (per-bit difficulty profile — refined inline). Built 4-bit-per-op extended VM (16 ops: 8 base {PUSH0/1/N, INC, ADD, SUB, MUL, SHR1, DUP, EMIT_S, EMIT0, HALT} + 4 R^{-1}-kernel arithmetic primitives {LOG2, LI_APPROX, DIV_LOG, GEO_SUM}) with integer stack alongside bit-emit stream; T_MAX = 4096, INT_CAP = 10⁹. C inner loop (`sim.c → sim.so`) batch-evaluates one program against all targets simultaneously; pre-skip of programs with no EMIT in pc cycle saves ~50% of enumeration. **Pre-stated falsifiers**: F1 (full shift to ⌈N/2⌉ — every easy-J compresses, every hard-J saturates); F2 (no shift — easy zone all saturated as in original VM, DUPLICATE-PLUS); F3 (intermediate hierarchy — some easy J compress, others saturate). **Result: F3 holds globally (intermediate hierarchy)**, with structure: per-N at L_max=24 (matched to target_lens 16/32/64), the cut moves fully to ⌈N/2⌉ for N ∈ {4, 5} and reverts to J*(N) for N=6; at L_max=28, N=6 partially shifts (J=4 compresses, J=3 still saturates). **Within-easy-zone J-monotone hierarchy identified**: bits closer to J*(N) (the trivial-zero boundary) compress at smaller L_max; bits closer to ⌈N/2⌉ (the E1.3 hard-easy boundary) require larger L_max — the bounded-Kt cost of bit-J of π is empirically monotone in N − J. **Headline compressing programs (L_max=24)**: (N=4, J=2) Kt_b'=33 prog `ADD, LI, LI, EMIT_S, PUSH_N, PUSH_N` — emits `bit_0(LI(LI(2x)))` which EXACTLY matches `bit_2(π(x))` on [0, 16); (N=5, J=3) Kt_b'=33 prog `EMIT_S, LI, DUP, INC, PUSH_N, PUSH0`. Triple-LI program `EMIT_S, PUSH_N, LI, LI, LI, DUP, EMIT_S` (L=28) compresses (N=6, J=4). **Falsified**: original C3 spec's S105 prediction "if YES, R^{-1}-kernel-equipped VM resolves the smooth/oscillatory transition" was correct AT SMALL N (4, 5) but breaks at N=6; the predicted full shift is L_max-budget limited. **Negative content**: hard-zone (J < ⌈N/2⌉) cells remain saturated at L_max ≤ target_len for every tested N ≥ 4; no compressing programs found within budget for hard bits. The structural orthogonality of Brandt's TRAVERSE to the per-bit family (all four obstructions O1-O4 of E5.8) is unaffected by VM choice — empirical compressibility of some `s_J^(N)` does not enable a Brandt diagonalisation. **Quantitative regime caveat**: at L_max > target_len the hard-easy distinction begins to fray (e.g. L_max=28 spuriously "compresses" N=4 hard zone J=0,1 because 28-bit programs can express any 16-bit pattern combinatorially); the meaningful regime is L_max ≤ target_len. **Refines E1.3 inline** with VM-richness hierarchy: 3-bit stack VM cuts at J*(N), 4-bit arith VM cuts at ⌈N/2⌉ for N ≤ 5 with within-easy-zone monotone J-ranking. Cross-domain ingredient: arithmetic-augmented bounded-Kt simulator (analogous to Levin Kt with non-trivial primitive set) — first project use of Li-kernel primitives inside Kt simulator. **Adds new finite-N empirical fact** (not previously measured): bounded-Kt cut location is VM-richness-AND-N-dependent with explicit hierarchy. Cites E5.8 (unchanged), E1.3 (refined inline), E1.5, E1.9 (LSB still saturates), E5.3. Successors proposed (S150): C3.a.i L_max=32 sweep (resolves N=6, J=3); C3.a.ii larger N at random-program sampling; C3.a.iii VM-budget vs RH-scale linkage to S146 F1 results; C3.a.iv ablation drop/swap of arithmetic primitives. See `experiments/constructions/brandt_per_bit_arith_vm/`, `archive/sessions/session150_c3a_arith_vm.md`. | 150 |
